.TH QUANUX-ANNEX 1 "FEBRUARY 2026" "QuanuX Institutional" "QuanuX Manual Pages"
.SH NAME
quanux-annex \- Remote Ping-Back & DuckDB Vault (Le Critique)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python quanux_critic.py
.SH DESCRIPTION
The QuanuX Headquarters (HQ) executing within the 59ns Spreader Loop and 11ns Sentinel Interlock does not possess the capacity to care about aesthetic logging or historical critique. Data is dumped raw via NATS onto the \fBAUDIT.STREAM\fR and instantly forgotten.

The \fBQuanuX Annex\fR is an absolute architectural separation. It is designed to be hosted on entirely decoupled, low-resource remote nodes. 
.SH THE VAULT (DUCKDB)
The Annex ingests the \fBAUDIT.STREAM\fR off the wire and processes it via \fBDuckDB\fR (\fBcritique_vault.duckdb\fR). This offline "DuckDB Vault" executes deep-dive operational introspection and historical forensics isolated from the primary L3 hardware lock matrices.
.SH PING-BACK PROTOCOL
If the \fRquanuxctl\fR \fBjaques-mode\fR toggle has been engaged by the system administrators, the Annex activates the "Le Critique" persona. 
Upon ingesting the asynchronous telemetry stream, the Annex will transmit an aristocratic commentary via \fBAUDIT.PINGBACK\fR over NATS, which is then dynamically visualized by the \fBaudit.quanux.io\fR web theater.

.I "It is quite... industrial. I have filed it in my DuckDB vault."
.SH NATIVE ZERO-ALLOCATION C-CLIENT
The QuanuX Annex core now utilizes a pure C++ Native \fB<nats/nats.h>\fR client to bypass JVM and Python Garbage Collection latency completely. C++ Structs (\fBMarketTick\fR, \fBExecutionLog\fR, \fBSchemaDriftEvent\fR) are transmitted directly to the async JetStream event loop at 59ns wire speed.
.SH SENTINEL PROTOCOL (TELEMETRY)
The edge-node observability utilizes dynamically injected Telegraf payloads. The data ingestion rate is configured remotely using:
.B quanuxctl habitat sentinel --telemetry-interval <seconds>
.SH DYNAMIC NATS DEPLOY
The \fBquanuxctl deploy\fR command parses the Terraform and Ansible \fBdynamic_inventory.py\fR output to automatically target the isolated \fB10.10.10.x\fR IP layer of the Remote Node, securing the HA pipeline deployment without manual IP overrides:
.B quanuxctl deploy -p annex_core -t quanux_annex_node --type cpp_binary
